WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.460 --> 00:00:03.320
- Welcome to the University of Georgia

00:00:03.320 --> 00:00:05.784
2020 virtual gradation ceremony.

00:00:05.784 --> 00:00:08.554
(fireworks exploding)

00:00:08.554 --> 00:00:12.210
(family cheering)

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:13.310
Turn you tassel again.

00:00:15.350 --> 00:00:16.437
- I know my kids one day will be like

00:00:16.437 --> 00:00:19.257
"Mom, you graduated during the pandemic?

00:00:19.257 --> 00:00:20.137
"What did you do?"

00:00:20.137 --> 00:00:22.069
And so I just think that's
going to be something

00:00:22.069 --> 00:00:23.873
that you're not going to forget.

00:00:23.873 --> 00:00:27.956
(speaking in a foreign language)

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:34.310
- [Narrator] As schools around the world

00:00:34.310 --> 00:00:36.810
are trying to figure out
what to do about graduation

00:00:36.810 --> 00:00:38.860
during the coronavirus pandemic

00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:41.663
some have moved ahead
with robots and avatars.

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:44.400
Here's how they seize the opportunity

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:45.563
and got creative.

00:00:47.470 --> 00:00:51.300
Ivan Campbell is a junior at
the University of Georgia.

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:53.300
- I know that if my graduation

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:56.340
were to suddenly not exist anymore

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:58.220
that I would be really
really hurt by that.

00:00:58.220 --> 00:01:00.970
- [Newscaster] Junior Ivan
Campbell got creative.

00:01:00.970 --> 00:01:02.430
- [Narrator] So he came up with the idea

00:01:02.430 --> 00:01:04.370
of holding a graduation ceremony

00:01:04.370 --> 00:01:06.830
in the video game Minecraft.

00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:08.860
It's where players can build 3D worlds

00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:11.420
with characters and experiences.

00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:15.960
- I think that to sort of
physically be in a space

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:16.810
with other people,

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:18.773
even if it's not really physical.

00:01:19.610 --> 00:01:23.860
I think that that brings
a lot to the experience.

00:01:23.860 --> 00:01:25.600
We have this really really big stadium

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:26.710
called Sanford Stadium.

00:01:26.710 --> 00:01:27.840
It's huge.

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:30.780
You know it can hold 50,000 people or so.

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:32.853
It's where we have our graduations.

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:34.690
- [Narrator] He knew he couldn't build

00:01:34.690 --> 00:01:36.530
the entire stadium alone

00:01:36.530 --> 00:01:39.210
and so Campbell teamed
up with other students.

00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:41.820
- [Ivan] We referenced a
lot of our school schematics

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:43.670
that they had laid out

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:47.300
and we also used Googlemaps
with those streetviews

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:50.540
to get an idea of what
the spacial dimensions

00:01:50.540 --> 00:01:52.880
need to look like within the game.

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:54.830
- [Narrator] Campbell says
there were lots of late nights

00:01:54.830 --> 00:01:56.290
with the team over the three weeks

00:01:56.290 --> 00:01:58.456
it took to build the stadium virtually.

00:01:58.456 --> 00:02:01.539
(country rock music)

00:02:05.070 --> 00:02:06.460
- And I've also become a little bit closer

00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:08.333
with a lot of the other people.

00:02:08.333 --> 00:02:11.610
It sort of brings us
together as a community.

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:13.437
- [Male GA Student] Good job Ivan.

00:02:13.437 --> 00:02:14.334
(fireworks going off)

00:02:14.334 --> 00:02:16.212
(students laughing and cheering)

00:02:16.212 --> 00:02:17.100
- [Narrator] Though the school is holding

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:18.970
the official ceremony in October

00:02:18.970 --> 00:02:22.200
the administration gave Campbell
the blessing to move ahead.

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:24.500
So on the big day more
than a dozen students

00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:25.390
got ready at home

00:02:25.390 --> 00:02:28.216
and showed up on the virtual campus.

00:02:28.216 --> 00:02:29.119
- Hey that's me!

00:02:29.119 --> 00:02:30.813
Astrophysics!

00:02:30.813 --> 00:02:32.211
Girl go!

00:02:32.211 --> 00:02:33.741
Ah!

00:02:33.741 --> 00:02:34.972
Hello!

00:02:34.972 --> 00:02:36.327
Let's give a jump.

00:02:36.327 --> 00:02:37.335
Ha!

00:02:37.335 --> 00:02:38.574
(Mackenzie laughing)

00:02:38.574 --> 00:02:42.110
Oh, she gave me a jump (laughing)

00:02:42.110 --> 00:02:44.180
- You are part of history.

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:46.948
This is a year no one will ever forget.

00:02:46.948 --> 00:02:48.691
♪ Let's go! ♪

00:02:48.691 --> 00:02:50.013
- [Ivan] Woo, you go to see the--

00:02:50.013 --> 00:02:51.765
- [Mackenzie] Makin
you run boy! (laughing)

00:02:51.765 --> 00:02:52.598
- [Ivan] Oh, that's so good.

00:02:52.598 --> 00:02:53.750
- [Maile] Just so really blew

00:02:53.750 --> 00:02:55.870
all that citations out the water.

00:02:55.870 --> 00:02:56.703
- [Male Student] Time is
something that is beginning

00:02:56.703 --> 00:02:57.536
to affect our--

00:02:57.536 --> 00:03:01.540
- Class of 2020 is going
to be very memorable.

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:04.518
I do not think we are
going to be forgotten.

00:03:04.518 --> 00:03:08.601
(speaking in a foreign language)

00:03:09.650 --> 00:03:12.100
- [Narrator] Some universities
have not wanted to postpone

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:14.160
or cancel ceremonies altogether.

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:17.370
So this school came up with
the idea of using robots.

00:03:17.370 --> 00:03:20.870
- Our BBT University is 100%

00:03:20.870 --> 00:03:21.703
online.

00:03:21.703 --> 00:03:23.930
- [Narrator] Shugo Yanaka is a professor

00:03:23.930 --> 00:03:26.576
at the Business Breakthrough
University in Tokyo.

00:03:26.576 --> 00:03:27.409
(tech music)

00:03:27.409 --> 00:03:30.530
- [Shugo] Our university
have the graduation ceremony

00:03:30.530 --> 00:03:31.740
once a year.

00:03:31.740 --> 00:03:32.920
It's in person.

00:03:32.920 --> 00:03:36.440
But this time the coronavirus situation,

00:03:36.440 --> 00:03:38.603
students couldn't come together.

00:03:39.710 --> 00:03:42.590
This truly online graduation
ceremony took place

00:03:42.590 --> 00:03:45.903
with the professor actually
present at the venue.

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:49.600
Just watching video is kind of boring,

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:52.450
but the other third
have a physical presence

00:03:52.450 --> 00:03:56.123
and making it seems like
human were actually there.

00:03:57.200 --> 00:03:58.770
- [Narrator] About a
100 graduates attended

00:03:58.770 --> 00:04:02.030
the virtual ceremony via video conference.

00:04:02.030 --> 00:04:04.120
Four of them were chosen
to represent the class

00:04:04.120 --> 00:04:06.913
and have their faces screened
onto the robot's heads.

00:04:07.837 --> 00:04:11.920
(speaking in a foreign language)

00:04:17.660 --> 00:04:19.890
Yanaka said he's gotten phone
calls from other schools

00:04:19.890 --> 00:04:23.250
about tips for holding a
graduation with robots.

00:04:23.250 --> 00:04:26.000
- [Shugo] We are facing
with difficult situation.

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:30.380
But I think it's a good
opportunities for us to

00:04:30.380 --> 00:04:33.433
discover the possibilities around us.

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:36.870
- [Narrator] Campbell has
noticed other students

00:04:36.870 --> 00:04:40.540
holding their own graduation
ceremonies in Minecraft.

00:04:40.540 --> 00:04:43.116
- [Ivan] So many people in
the comments supported us.

00:04:43.116 --> 00:04:45.830
It's really really nice to
have people getting together

00:04:45.830 --> 00:04:48.336
in a time when people are apart.

00:04:48.336 --> 00:04:49.483
♪ To Georgia ♪

00:04:49.483 --> 00:04:50.673
- [Maile] It's kind of a joke right?

00:04:50.673 --> 00:04:51.910
Where graduating--

00:04:51.910 --> 00:04:53.043
- [Female Student] Yay '20.

00:04:54.010 --> 00:04:54.910
That's right baby!

